        {
          "ruleId": "CWE-444",
          "level": "error",
          "message": {
            "text": "HTTP request smuggling (CWE-444) via non-RFC chunk sizes in ChunkedReader.parse_chunk_size: line 88 computes `chunk_size = line.split(b\";\",1)[0].strip()` and line 90 parses it with `int(chunk_size, 16)`, whose only guard is `except ValueError` (line 92). Python's int(x,16) accepts forms that RFC 7230 chunk-size forbids: a leading sign (`int(b\"-1\",16) == -1`), an explicit `0x` prefix (`int(b\"0x10\",16) == 16`), and PEP-515 underscores (`int(b\"1_0\",16) == 16`). There is NO `chunk_size < 0` check -- line 94 only tests `if chunk_size == 0:` (which is the branch that consumes trailers and returns (0,None)), so a negative size falls through to line 100 `return (chunk_size, rest_chunk)`. In parse_chunked the loop head is line 59 `while size > 0:`, so a negative size exits the loop immediately and the body generator terminates WITHOUT ever validating a terminating 0-length chunk; the unconsumed socket bytes stay buffered in the unreader and are parsed as the next pipelined request on the keep-alive connection. Attack: send `Transfer-Encoding: chunked` with a first chunk-size line of `-1` (or `0x10`/`1_0`), followed by a smuggled request -- any front-end proxy that rejects or differently interprets these forms desynchronizes from gunicorn.\n\nVerifier (CONFIRM): Independently verified in the real source (gunicorn 21.2.0). gunicorn/http/body.py:88-100 parses the chunk-size with `int(chunk_size, 16)` guarded only by `except ValueError`, with no hexdigit-only validation (repo-wide grep for `0123456789abcdef|hexdigits|CHUNK_SIZE|chunk_size` found no validator; the only other hits are response-side writers util.py:291 and wsgi.py:372). Python's int(x,16) accepts forms RFC 9112 S7.1 (`chunk-size = 1*HEXDIG`) forbids: a leading sign (`-1` -> -1), an explicit `0x` prefix (`0x10` -> 16), and PEP-515 underscores (`1_0` -> 16); `.strip()` on line 88 additionally eats \\t\\r\\n\\x0b\\x0c. Line 94 tests only `chunk_size == 0`, so a negative value falls through to line 100 `return (chunk_size, rest_chunk)`. In parse_chunked the loop head at line 59 is `while size > 0:`, so size=-1 skips the body entirely: the chunk terminator check (lines 71-72 `rest[:2] != b'\\r\\n'` -> ChunkMissingTerminator) and the 0-chunk/trailer path (94-99) never run, and no exception is raised. Body.read (177-224) -> ChunkedReader.read (19-39) gets StopIteration on the first next() and returns b\"\", so the request is served as a well-formed body-less request. gunicorn/http/parser.py:34-42 then drains the (empty) body and parses the NEXT request off the SAME unreader/socket, and message.py:156-165 should_close() returns False for HTTP/1.1 without Connection: close -- a textbook TE-desync primitive against any front-end that forwards or interprets these non-RFC chunk-size forms differently. Reach confirmed: message.py:134-139 builds ChunkedReader for any `Transfer-Encoding: chunked`, and the graph reports parse_chunk_size and parse_chunked with reachable_from_entry=true, hop_distance=1. Two corrections to the analyst: (1) the already-recv'd bytes in `rest_chunk` are DISCARDED, not re-buffered -- parse_chunked never calls unreader.unread(rest) when the loop is skipped -- so prefix injection requires the smuggled request to land past the 8192-byte SocketUnreader read boundary (unreader.py:58), which is attacker-paddable and routine when a proxy writes headers and body separately; (2) the default sync worker force_closes every connection (sync.py:173), so the back-end second-request path needs gthread/gevent/eventlet keepalive (base_async.py:39-48, gthread.py:329-332). Neither voids the defect. exploit_search returned \"exploit corpus unavailable: not indexed\", so severity is derived from the code, not from a matched Metasploit module; version is pinned exactly at 21.2.0 (gunicorn/__init__.py:6 `version_info = (21, 2, 0)`; docs/source/news.rst:5 \"21.2.0 - 2023-07-19\" is the newest entry), i.e. this tree predates the upstream 22.0.0 request-smuggling hardening and contains no chunk-size allowlist."
          },
